# How to cite sand3d: GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository". The README's BibTeX says the same.
# Version and date are those of the public release, 1.6.3: update both at each public release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sand3d in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sand3d"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for writing 3D objects as programs. A program describes how a shape is
  made, in profiles, solids, edits, frames and assemblies, and Blender (bpy) computes the
  geometry.
authors:
  - given-names: "Thibault"
    family-names: "Neveu"
    email: "thibault.neveu@sandflow.ai"
    affiliation: "Sandflow"
  - given-names: "Andréa"
    family-names: "Loy"
    affiliation: "Sandflow"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.6.3
date-released: 2026-11-06
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sandflow-ai/sand3d"
keywords:
  - 3D
  - procedural modeling
  - CAD
  - code generation
  - Blender
